{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"Knowledge Bases for Amazon Bedrock now lets you configure inference parameters","context":"Amazon Bedrock's Knowledge Bases now enable users to configure inference parameters for foundation models, providing greater control over the responses' randomness, diversity, length, and output. Users can adjust temperature and top-p settings to make the model more or less random and consider fewer or more word options","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2024/05/knowledge-bases-amazon-bedrock-configure-parameters/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"aws-ai-ml","skill_description":"Selects, deploys, and customizes AI models on Amazon SageMaker. Training or Processing jobs, fine-tuning (SFT/DPO/RLVR/RLAIF), model selection, evaluation, SageMaker or Bedrock deployment, inference optimization and endpoint diagnostics. Use when fine-tuning models on SageMaker, choosing a base model to customize or deploy from SageMaker JumpStart or Hub, SageMakerPublicHub, or the model catalog, checking data quality (duplicates, languages, PII), transforming or validating data (reformat, clean, filter, dedupe, split, merge, redact), generating synthetic data, labeling data with a model, human review or annotation and applying its corrections, evaluating model quality, deploying or optimizing endpoints, configuring IAM/S3, or managing SageMaker Managed MLflow. Use for endpoint health, latency, logs, metrics, errors. Covers Serverless Model Customization, Nova and OSS deployment paths, and PySDK v3. NOT for SageMaker Ground Truth labeling jobs, Feature Store, or general AWS infrastructure.\n\nServices: sagemaker, s3, iam, bedrock\nTasks: build, deploy, debug, optimize\nPersona: developer, data-scientist\nWorkload: ai-ml","skill_name":"aws-ai-ml"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"amazon-bedrock","skill_description":"Builds generative AI applications on Amazon Bedrock. Covers model invocation (Converse API, InvokeModel), RAG with Knowledge Bases, Bedrock Agents, Guardrails, and AgentCore (including the Harness managed agent loop). Applies when invoking models, setting up or migrating Knowledge Bases to Managed, deploying to AgentCore, migrating/porting/converting a Bedrock Agent (including inline agents) to an AgentCore Harness, troubleshooting Bedrock errors (ThrottlingException, AccessDeniedException), or choosing Bedrock models (Claude, Llama, Nova, Titan). Also for prompt caching, quota and throttling diagnosis, cost tracking, migrating between Claude model generations, chunking strategies, and Bedrock model selection. Covers AgentCore Payments (x402, microtransactions, Payment Manager, Connector, Instrument, Coinbase CDP, Stripe Privy, paid endpoints, agent payments). NOT for custom model training, Rekognition, or Comprehend. For SageMaker model discovery, customization, or endpoints, use aws-ai-ml.\n\nServices: bedrock, bedrock-runtime, bedrock-mantle, bedrock-agent, bedrock-agent-runtime, bedrock-agentcore-control, bedrock-agentcore\nTasks: deploy, debug, optimize, design, migrate\nPersona: developer, devops, architect\nWorkload: generative-ai, rag, agents","skill_name":"amazon-bedrock"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"writing-agentcore-policy","skill_description":"Authors, validates and submits Amazon Bedrock AgentCore Policy statements (Cedar and Dogwood) for an AgentCore Gateway. Discovers the Gateway's targets and tools, generates the Gateway's Cedar schema, drafts permit/forbid, guardrail and temporal policies from access requirements or from a whole natural-language policy document (splitting it into rules, marking the rules that cannot be expressed, and repairing failing drafts in batches), checks them locally (syntax, schema, API limits, claim and guardrail pitfalls), and creates or updates them in a policy engine after explicit developer approval, reporting the final status and service findings. Use when a developer wants to write, translate, fix, validate or submit AgentCore Gateway policies, convert a policy document or a list of rules into policies, restrict which users or roles can call Gateway tools, add Bedrock guardrail or session-history (temporal) conditions, or resolve CreatePolicy/UpdatePolicy failures.\n\nServices: bedrock-agentcore-control, bedrock-agentcore\nTasks: design, deploy, debug, secure\nPersona: developer, security\nWorkload: agents, generative-ai","skill_name":"writing-agentcore-policy"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Look up Bedrock inference parameters for determinism"}
